<section class="in subpage">
  <p class="kicker">Welcome to MusicMentor by Joshua Ediale</p>
  <h1>You're in. Thank you.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Most singers wait for a better voice, a bigger stage or the "right time" before they work on their craft. You didn't wait. You signed up because you value insight, and you know insight is only worth something when you act on it.</p>
  <p>That's the kind of singer I write for. MusicMentor won't flatter you. Some notes will challenge habits you've had for years, and some will ask you to practise things that feel small and boring. The singers who keep growing are the ones who do that work when nobody is clapping.</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What you'll get</h2>
  <ul class="perks">
    <li><strong>A round-up every Tuesday and Friday.</strong> The new notes on your voice, your team and your congregation, in one short email. No need to go looking.</li>
    <li><strong>First access.</strong> When I release a guide, a training or a new resource for singers, subscribers hear first, before I announce it anywhere else.</li>
    <li><strong>Notes I only send by email.</strong> Now and then, something short that doesn't make it to the blog.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I won't flood your inbox, and I'll never sell or share your email. Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link.</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Who's writing</h2>
  <p>I'm Joshua Ediale, a worship leader, singer, songwriter and vocal coach. I've led music since 2009, from Warri to CFI UNIBEN, and today I serve as a lead vocalist and music minister at RHOGIC Abuja. I wrote <em>The Lead Singer's Handbook</em>.</p>
  <p>A personal welcome email from me will reach you in the next few minutes. If it lands in Promotions, drag it to Primary so you don't miss the next one.</p>
